.TH TULPAR-MARK 1 "2026" "tulpar 0.7.0" "Tulpar Manual"
.SH NAME
tulpar-mark \- mark a package as automatic or explicit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tulpar mark
.RI [ options "] (" \-\-auto " | " \-\-explicit ") " name ...
.br
.B tulpar m
.RI [ options "] (" \-\-auto " | " \-\-explicit ") " name ...
.br
.B tulpar \-m
.RI [ options "] (" \-\-auto " | " \-\-explicit ") " name ...
.SH DESCRIPTION
Changes whether installed packages count as installed explicitly or as
dependencies. Packages marked automatic become candidates for removal
by
.BR tulpar-orphans (1)
once nothing requires them; explicit packages are never treated as
orphans. Requires root privileges unless
.B \-\-dest
points to a user-owned root.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-auto
Mark the packages as installed automatically, as dependencies.
.TP
.B \-\-explicit
Mark the packages as installed explicitly.
.TP
.BR \-d ", " \-\-dest " " \fIpath\fR
Operate on the database of an alternate root.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 on success, 1 if any package is not installed or neither or both of
.B \-\-auto
and
.B \-\-explicit
are given.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR tulpar (1),
.BR tulpar-why (1),
.BR tulpar-orphans (1)
